import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest.UseMainMethod;

@SpringBootTest(useMainMethod = UseMainMethod.ALWAYS)
class MyApplicationTests {

	@Test
	void exampleTest() {
		// ...
	}

}
```

With this setting, the profiles that `main` sets are active when the context starts [S1].

There are two options for `useMainMethod`:
- **`ALWAYS`**: the test fails if no `main` method can be found [S1].
- **`WHEN_AVAILABLE`**: the test uses `main` if it exists. Otherwise it falls back to the standard loading mechanism [S1].

