The imported top-level `@TestConfiguration` is processed first. It is processed before the nested `@TestConfiguration`, and before any configuration found through component scanning [S2].

Usually this makes no noticeable difference. It can matter if you rely on bean overriding, because the order decides which definition gets processed first [S2]. The docs don't say more about which definition wins in that case. If both configurations define the same bean, I'd avoid depending on the order. Give the beans distinct names, or define the bean in only one place.

Here is how the two kinds of configuration are used:
- A nested `@TestConfiguration` is used in addition to your application's primary configuration. It doesn't replace that configuration, which a nested `@Configuration` would [S1].
- A top-level `@TestConfiguration` is not picked up by scanning. You have to import it explicitly [S2]:

```java
@SpringBootTest
@Import(MyTestsConfiguration.class)
class MyTests { }
```

