**Mocking a collaborator**

Put `@MockitoBean` on a field in the test class. It replaces the bean in the `ApplicationContext` with a Mockito mock. `@WebMvcTest` is usually limited to a single controller, and `@MockitoBean` supplies mocks for that controller's collaborators [S4, S8]. The example below is from the docs:

```java
@WebMvcTest(UserVehicleController.class)
class MyControllerTests {

	@Autowired
	private MockMvcTester mvc;

	@MockitoBean
	private UserVehicleService userVehicleService;

	@Test
	void testExample() {
		given(this.userVehicleService.getVehicleDetails("sboot"))
			.willReturn(new VehicleDetails("Honda", "Civic"));
		assertThat(this.mvc.get().uri("/sboot/vehicle").accept(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN))
			.hasStatusOk()
			.hasBodyTextEqualTo("Honda Civic");
	}
}
```

The imports are `org.springframework.test.context.bean.override.mockito.MockitoBean` and `org.mockito.BDDMockito.given` [S2]. If you need a spy instead of a mock, use `@MockitoSpyBean` [S8].

