The `@DataJpaTest` documentation says:

- **Transactions:** Data JPA tests are transactional and roll back at the end of each test by default [S4]. The docs don't say how `@Sql` interacts with that transaction. Check the Spring Framework docs on whether `@Sql` scripts run inside it and get rolled back.
- **Opting out of the transaction:** you can disable it for a test or a whole class with `@Transactional(propagation = Propagation.NOT_SUPPORTED)` [S4]:

```java
@DataJpaTest
@Transactional(propagation = Propagation.NOT_SUPPORTED)
class MyNonTransactionalTests {
	// ...
}
```

- **Database:** an embedded database is used by default if one is on the classpath [S4]. To run against a real database, add `@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = Replace.NONE)` [S3].
- **Seeding without scripts:** the documented approach is to inject `TestEntityManager` and call `persist(...)` in the test [S3]. A `JdbcTemplate` is also available if you want to run SQL directly [S3].
